        <head>INFLUENZA.</head>
        <p>INFLUENZA.</p>
        <p>(La Grippe). There can be little doubt that Influenza is as prevalent now in this country' as it has ever been, but as we are more accustomed to it, it attracts less attention. The symptoms are so well known as t 3 require no description, but the causes are less understood. It is, however, certain that when the system has run down and is in what is termed a low condition, that it is peculiarly liable to an attack of INFLUENZA, on LA GRIPPE. Yaw remedies have been suggested, but it is gener- ally acknowledged that the best treatment is nourishing food, warmth, and a good tonic. 'the best tonic is -QUININE. And it has been clearly demonstrated that the best and most effective way of administering Quinine is the formof GWILYM EVANS' QUININE ffirrEits. These Bitters have many advantages, which are now fully recognised :- 1. They are PURELY VEGE I'A.BLE, and are a plea- sant and safe way of taking Quinine. 2. They have stood the test of TWENTY YEARS, and are acknowledged to be a HAPPY CO7II3INATIO' of the Best Medicinal Plants yet discovered ; such as Quinine. Sarsaparilla, Lavender, Gentian, 'Dandelion, &amp;c., mixed in scientific proportions, and forming a fonic prepara- tion which is ABSOLUTELY UNEQUALLED. 3. We claim that by taking a dose of these Quinine Bitten daily, say about 11 o'clock, and thus keeping the system in good order. INFLUENZA CAN BE KEPT OFF. 4. We also claim that after an attack of Influenza, when the patient is suffering from extreme weakness, lassitude, and low spirits, there is no preparation yet dis- covered equal to GWILYM EVANS' QUININE BITTERS. To strengthen the system and revive the spirits. ONE WORD OF CAUTION. All good things, whether in medicine or anything else,' are now imitated ; and the great success of Gqvilym Evans' Quinine Bitters has been the means of starting many imitations which are absolutely of no value com- pared with these Bitters. The only advantage offered as an inducement to buy them, le,—that they are cheaper. This we admit, but assert that worrrimEss imitations ARE DEAR AT ANY PRICE. We hold ourselves responsible for every package, which bears the name Gwilym Evans on the stamp, label and bottle, and for no other. Sold by all Chemists, in bottl :s at 23. 9d. and 4s. 61 each, sample bottles at is. 1 I. QUININE BITTERS MANUFACTURING CO., LTD., LLANELLI', SOUTII WALES.</p>
