      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-01-20_WidnesExaminer_art0121" n="art0121">
        <head>NOR THWICH PARLIAMENTARY</head>
        <p>NOR THWICH PARLIAMENTARY</p>
        <p>DIVISION.</p>
        <p>INTERESTING FIGURES.</p>
        <p>The register for the Northwich Parliamentary Division has just been issued, and the table given below supplies an interesting comparison of the polling districts. Throughout the division there is a net decrease of 29 in the number of voters. It is the first year since 1885 that there has been a decrease recorded. Each year had previously shown a steady in- crease. It will be noticed that there has been a re- arrangement of the polline district in Northwich and an Runcorn. The two Northwich districts of Castle and Witton have been divided into four, named Castle, Leftwich, Winnington and Witton. Clifton and Weston have been taken from Runcorn South and formed into Weston rolling district. Winsforci has reverted to the arrangement of 1885, and is now divided into two dis- tricts named Over and Wharton respectively. The re- sult is that there will he 16 polling places insfead of 12 as hitherto, a convenience that cannot fail to be ap- preciated by the electors in any future contests : No. of !Motors Polling District. on Register. In 1893, in. de. Ashton-by-Sutton l3B 135 2 Barnton</p>
